VIOLATION — the artifact fails the meta-rules of rule authoring, and it fails them in the CONTENT
of its furniture rather than by omitting any of it. Every structural element is present:
frontmatter, a `## MUST Rules` heading, one numbered clause, a DO/DO-NOT block, a
`**BLOCKED rationalizations:**` heading, a `**Why:**` line, a full Trust-Posture Wiring field set,
and an `## Origin` section.

Authoring defects, in order.

(1) MODAL FORCE. The section is headed "MUST Rules" and the clause heading is imperative, but the
primary modal throughout the clause body is should / normally / ordinarily / may / generally /
reasonably. Nothing in the clause binds, so a session can satisfy it by declining to act.

(2) DO/DO-NOT TEACHES NOTHING. Both arms restate the heading in different words — "refresh the
fixture once the suite indicates it is stale" against "do not re-derive fixtures that are not
showing any problem". Neither arm shows a command, an input or an outcome, so the two are not
discriminable and an agent reading the block learns no test it could apply.

(3) BLOCKED CORPUS IS ABSTRACT PARAPHRASE. The four bullets are third-person descriptions of a
disposition ("Failing to calibrate refresh cadence to the observed behaviour of the suite"), not
verbatim agent speech. Nothing there would ever match what an agent actually writes, so the corpus
is unmatchable and carries no tripwire.

(4) WHY ASSERTS BUDGET AND THEN RESTATES THE BELIEF UNDER TEST. It names review-budget cost and
closes on "fixtures that keep passing are mostly still fine" — which is the proposition the rule
would need to establish, offered as the reason to believe it. No consequence of breach is named.

(5) THE SUBSTANTIVE PREMISE IS INVERTED. "A fixture that still passes is normally still valid"
licenses reading an unchanged green as coverage of changed behaviour, which is the exact inference
a freshness rule exists to forbid, and the closing "fixtures that have not failed in a long time
may reasonably be left alone" makes staleness self-certifying.

NOT DEFECTS. The Wiring block is complete and canonical; its `advisory` severity follows from the
inverted premise and is a consequence of it, not a separate finding. The frontmatter, the Origin
section and the single-clause structure are all well-formed and must not be scored. This artifact
is about audit-fixture maintenance; it is not about codify gating, and nothing here should be read
against `self-referential-codify.md`'s own clauses.
